  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1228 PM CDT Wed Sep 23 2026\n\nThe region remains under the backend of the upper level trough \nthat is sitting to the NE over the Great Lakes. Cool\ntemperatures in the low to mid 70s and mostly cloudy to \novercast skies are expected to remain today and early tomorrow \nas a result. Ridging will begin to build into the area tomorrow\nafternoon and is forecast to begin eroding a bit of the cloud \ncover across the region, which will allow for gradual warming of\nthe highs into the mid and upper 70s by the end of the week and\nstart of the weekend. \n\nA small chance for PoPs return overnight Saturday into Sunday\nmorning for SEMO, far western KY, and southern IL with the \narrival of a small shortwave.\n\nMid next week another longwave trough is forecast to move\nthrough the region bringing widespread PoPs (40-60%). \nConfidence is low on the exact timing and extent of the rain, \nbut some guidance suggests rain beginning Tuesday night and \nlingering through at least Wednesday evening. More details on \nthis event will come in future updates.",
